From 24117cbbc7c5f2965ec1b47d1ba3cd75fb02ef8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy <andylee77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:44:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] detection: one Detection page, detectd and its event
 front end; a labelled preview overlay

raptor's IVS detection could be set in raptor.conf alone, what it found
showed only as rod's unlabelled boxes in the sub stream, and it reached no
event target.

- A new package, thingino-detect, which raptor's IVS build option selects:
  - Settings > Detection (config-detect.html): status, on and off, the
    method (the ones whose libraries the image has), the model, its class
    count, confidence, overlap and inference rate, the boxes, the event
    targets. A save writes only what changed; when the camera stages a
    setting for a restart, the page offers it. The page also serves
    thingino-ipud, from its plugin flags, so it is one page for both
    detectors.
  - detectd reads rvd's detections over raptor's control socket
    (raptor-ipc) and publishes them through one event front end
    (detfront.c): a status file, a socket, MQTT, ONVIF events, Home
    Assistant and Frigate, set up from the "detect" block of
    /etc/thingino.json by detect-events. It starts with S36detectd and
    follows rvd through a raptor.d hook. The publishers keep thingino-ipud's
    names (/usr/libexec/ipud-onvif, -ha, -frigate) so a controller sees one
    kind of camera.
- The preview gets a Detections button: boxes with the class name and score
  over the picture, for the viewer alone, fed by json-detect.cgi as one
  server-sent event stream while it is on; no boxes are drawn over a player
  without a picture.
- detect-overlay.js draws for both detectors: thingino-ipud's overlay was the
  same code, so preview-ipud.js now only feeds it from its own event stream.
  Same button, same remembered choice.

thingino-ipud's own move to the shared page and front end is not in this
series. The overlay and its feed have run on an Ingenic T31 camera with
detection on, the boxes following at a median of 360 ms; the page, with a
model taken from the SD card, on the same camera. On the emulated T41 the
page's save, detectd's start from it, its ONVIF event and its restart by the
raptor.d hook work; detectd with real objects on a camera, and its outputs
against a live Home Assistant or Frigate, were not run (a host test covers
them with canned rvd replies). The two
raptor patches that let rod's boxes reach the sub stream at all are 0112 and
0113 of the Thingino series.
